A||||5||Fierochic88||Rim Cleaning - Need Help||||1||
Z||000000||Fierochic88||11-27-2001||08:35 PM||||Hello all -<BR>   It seems like many of us out there have those grey 15" diamond spoke rims.  I have a set of a car right now that are pretty filthy.  I need to get them really clean and am looking to see if there is a better way to do it.  Currently TooManyFieros and I are using a special drill bit and a tire brush with about the same success, the drill bit is easier to me.  The problem is finding a good cleaning product to get the interior of the spokes really clean.  We have tried PrepSol, GoofOff, Mother's Aluminum/Mag Polish, Buffing Compound and one or two other products.  The Mag Polish and Prep Sol work the best, but still not too great.  Does anyone have any suggestions to shine up those rims without totally breaking our backs?  Thanks much!<P>Jennifer <P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.personal.psu.edu/users/j/j/jjr161/Fierochic88Signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||LoW_KeY||11-27-2001||09:17 PM||||Ahh yes, don't forget us with the black rims   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I went to the MI show and about died, they were so clean! I can wax mine and all and they only look good for a few days   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <P>I plan on getting them powder coated gloss black, but someone share a secret   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>My outter lips of my rims look like chrome when polished up, but that horrid black Grrr!<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by LoW_KeY (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||Formula88||11-27-2001||09:28 PM||||You're using some of the same products I am, so no help there.  There doesn't seem to be an easy way to clean them.  I'm also planning on stripping and powder coating mine in the future.  That should be an easier to care for finish.  Get the rim polished up real good, strip the black off, then have the center powder coated gloss black and the entire wheel powder coated clear - if you can do that.  <P>If I get my 17's this winter, my Diamond Spokes will be reserved for shows - so I want them to look perfect!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||11-27-2001||11:08 PM||||my 85 gt had those, major dirt, couldn't get it off AT ALL.. .EXCEPT!<P>spray on (and alot of it) Eagle One etching Mag Restorer (do'nt breathe this stuff), spray it and LEAVE it for 5 minutes then spray off, do it again and again, each time you spray it on use a brush and brush it in... again don't breath it... you'll find out why.  Turned mine into factory beautiful.||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||11-28-2001||05:58 AM||||One of the nice things about my 17s is that I clean them with just a little Formula 2001 and a rag  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Try some Formula 2001 on your stock wheels though, it sure works wonders going through grease on my 17s.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000005||LoW_KeY||11-28-2001||07:26 AM||||Will do! <P>I just hate buying product after product I love hearing feedback about it first, thanks.<P>-KC||||reg||14
